---
title: "getAccountLiquidity (Compound Whitepaper)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_init: comptroller.getAccountLiquidity(account) called
    q_init --> q_iter_markets: sumCollateral = 0; sumBorrow = 0
    q_iter_markets --> q_get_balance: for each market in account entered markets
    q_get_balance --> q_get_price: cTokenBalance = cToken.balanceOf(account); borrowBalance = cToken.borrowBalanceCurrent(account)
    q_get_price --> q_calc_collateral: price = oracle.getUnderlyingPrice(cToken)
    q_calc_collateral --> q_add_collateral: collateralValue = cTokenBalance * exchangeRate * price * collateralFactor
    q_add_collateral --> q_add_borrow: sumCollateral = sumCollateral + collateralValue
    q_add_borrow --> q_iter_markets: sumBorrow = sumBorrow + borrowBalance * price
    q_add_borrow --> q_compute_result: all markets processed
    q_compute_result --> q_surplus: sumCollateral > sumBorrow (account is healthy)
    q_compute_result --> q_shortfall: sumBorrow >= sumCollateral (account is underwater)
    q_surplus --> [*]: return (0, sumCollateral - sumBorrow, 0)
    q_shortfall --> [*]: return (0, 0, sumBorrow - sumCollateral)

    note right of q_calc_collateral
        INV-001: collateralFactor is in range [0, 1] per market
        INV-002: collateralValue = cTokenBalance * exchangeRate * oraclePrice * collateralFactor
    end note

    note right of q_compute_result
        INV-003: account is liquidatable if and only if sumBorrow > sumCollateral (shortfall > 0)
        INV-004: no action may increase shortfall (borrow, redeem, transfer cTokens blocked when shortfall > 0)
    end note

    note right of q_get_price
        INV-005: oracle price must be non-zero for all markets used as collateral
        INV-006: oracle price must be fresh (within acceptable staleness threshold)
    end note
